{"success": true, "message": "Test details sent successfully", "data": {"test": {"_id": "69de21f67e39d99b57bc5b5c", "analysisVideoCdn": "yt", "exam": ["605dfcb2f226ac25a8bd5fef"], "ctype": null, "position": 0, "order": 12, "enableCalculator": false, "isContinuousQuestion": false, "reattemptAvailable": false, "singleSectionMultipleSubjects": false, "timeRestricted": false, "title": "Thermodynamics (C) - Test 3", "description": "Previous Year Questions as Chapter Test", "syllabus": "This test contains questions from all topics of this chapter included in the JEE Main syllabus. It includes a mix of questions from PYQs of JEE Main 2019 - 2025.", "totalTime": 37, "totalQuestions": 25, "totalMarks": 100, "bonusQuestions": null, "bonusMarks": null, "startDate": "2026-04-15T03:30:00.000Z", "endDate": "2027-04-30T00:00:00.000Z", "type": "free", "class": "605df635a37b7025c438d685", "instruction": "608289ffb160b022e9442c83", "subjects": [{"subjectId": "607018ee404ae53194e73d91", "totalMarks": 100, "bonusMarks": 0, "totalQuestions": 25, "bonusQuestions": 0, "_id": "69de4f97e3e37d7ebba3bce4"}], "sections": [{"sectionId": {"_id": "69de4f97e3e37d7ebba3bc9f", "title": "Chemistry Single Correct", "sectionType": "normal", "subject": "607018ee404ae53194e73d91", "questions": [{"_id": "69de4f97e3e37d7ebba3bc38", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0df8c"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b476e"], "concepts": ["6162fb896ed13040ec850107"], "question": {"text": "A liquid when kept inside a thermally insulated closed vessel at $25^{\\circ} \\mathrm{C}$ was mechanically stirred from outside. What will be the correct option for the following thermodynamic parameters ?"}, "options": [{"id": "d41088", "text": "$\\Delta \\mathrm{U} \\lt 0, \\mathrm{q}=0, \\mathrm{w}\\gt0$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f97e3e37d7ebba3bc39"}, {"id": "f80c4e", "text": "$\\Delta \\mathrm{U}=0, \\mathrm{q}=0, \\mathrm{w}=0$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f97e3e37d7ebba3bc3a"}, {"id": "e37bbe", "text": "$\\Delta \\mathrm{U}\\gt0, \\mathrm{q}=0, \\mathrm{w}\\gt0$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f97e3e37d7ebba3bc3b"}, {"id": "378556", "text": "$\\Delta \\mathrm{U}=0, \\mathrm{q} \\lt 0, \\mathrm{w}\\gt0$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f97e3e37d7ebba3bc3c"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f97e3e37d7ebba3bc3d", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0df8c"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b4783"], "concepts": ["60e40fd4f1ef260f84ed1e51"], "question": {"text": "The difference between <math><mo>&#8710;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi></math> and <math><mo>&#8710;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">U</mi></math> is <math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mo>&#8710;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mo>-</mo><mo>&#8710;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">U</mi></mrow></mfenced></math>, when the combustion of one mole of heptane <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">l</mi></mfenced></math> is carried out at a temperature <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi></math> , is equal to:"}, "options": [{"id": "167a13", "text": "<math><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f97e3e37d7ebba3bc3e"}, {"id": "47f6fc", "text": "<math><mn>3</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f97e3e37d7ebba3bc3f"}, {"id": "09b1ea", "text": "<math><mn>4</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f97e3e37d7ebba3bc40"}, {"id": "0eaa51", "text": "<math><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f97e3e37d7ebba3bc41"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f97e3e37d7ebba3bc42", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0df8c"], "topics": ["60e2fb2066f9ce3f243b4b70"], "concepts": ["6117b8e067dbe2603c3e8ad2"], "question": {"text": "The entropy change associated with the conversion of <math><mn>1</mn><mi>&#160;</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>g</mi></math> of ice at <math><mn>273</mn><mi>&#160;</mi><mi>K</mi></math> to water vapours at <math><mn>383</mn><mi>&#160;</mi><mi>K</mi></math> is:<br /><br />(Specific heat of water liquid and water vapour are <math><mn>4.2</mn><mi>&#160;</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>J</mi><mi>&#160;</mi><msup><mrow><mi>K</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo></mrow></msup></math> and <math><mn>2.0</mn><mi>&#160;</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>J</mi><mi>&#160;</mi><msup><mrow><mi>K</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mi>k</mi><msup><mrow><mi>g</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math> ; heat of liquid fusion and vaporization of water are <math><mn>334</mn><mi>&#160;</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>J</mi><mi>&#160;</mi><mi>k</mi><msup><mrow><mi>g</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math> and <math><mn>2491</mn><mi>&#160;</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>J</mi><mi>&#160;</mi><mi>k</mi><msup><mrow><mi>g</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math> , respectively). ( <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">l</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">o</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></math> <math><mn>273</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>2.436</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">log</mi></mrow><mo>&#8289;</mo><mrow><mn>373</mn></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>2.572</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">log</mi></mrow><mo>&#8289;</mo><mrow><mn>383</mn></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>2.583</mn></math> )"}, "options": [{"id": "7b6636", "text": "<math><mn>9.26</mn><mi>&nbsp;</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>J</mi><mi>&nbsp;</mi><mi>k</mi><msup><mrow><mi>g</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><msup><mrow><mi>K</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f97e3e37d7ebba3bc43"}, {"id": "53c147", "text": "<math><mn>2.64</mn><mi> </mi><mi>k</mi><mi>J</mi><mi> </mi><mi>k</mi><msup><mrow><mi>g</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><msup><mrow><mi>K</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f97e3e37d7ebba3bc44"}, {"id": "acf04b", "text": "<math><mn>8.49</mn><mi> </mi><mi>k</mi><mi>J</mi><mi> </mi><mi>k</mi><msup><mrow><mi>g</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><msup><mrow><mi>K</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f97e3e37d7ebba3bc45"}, {"id": "31d9c1", "text": "<math><mn>7.90</mn><mi> </mi><mi>k</mi><mi>J</mi><mi> </mi><mi>k</mi><msup><mrow><mi>g</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><msup><mrow><mi>K</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f97e3e37d7ebba3bc46"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f97e3e37d7ebba3bc47", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0df8c"], "topics": ["60e5671c499d1e49588f8808"], "concepts": ["60e5671a499d1e49588f87ea"], "question": {"text": "Let us consider an endothermic reaction which is non-spontaneous at the freezing point of water. However, the reaction is spontaneous at boiling point of water. Choose the correct option."}, "options": [{"id": "053d90", "text": "Both $\\Delta \\mathrm{H}$ and $\\Delta \\mathrm{S}$ are (-ve)", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f97e3e37d7ebba3bc48"}, {"id": "195656", "text": "$\\Delta \\mathrm{H}$ is (-ve) but $\\Delta \\mathrm{S}$ is (+ve)", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f97e3e37d7ebba3bc49"}, {"id": "97ca59", "text": "$\\Delta \\mathrm{H}$ is $(+\\mathrm{ve})$ but $\\Delta \\mathrm{S}$ is $(-\\mathrm{ve})$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f97e3e37d7ebba3bc4a"}, {"id": "d88333", "text": "Both $\\Delta \\mathrm{H}$ and $\\Delta \\mathrm{S}$ are (+ve)", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f97e3e37d7ebba3bc4b"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f97e3e37d7ebba3bc4c", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0df8c"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b4783"], "concepts": ["60e2fad966f9ce3f243b473a"], "question": {"text": "If $\\quad C$ (diamond $) \\rightarrow C$ (graphite $)+\\mathrm{X} \\mathrm{kJ} \\mathrm{mol}^{-1}$\n$\\mathrm{C}($ diamond $)+\\mathrm{O}_2(\\mathrm{~g}) \\rightarrow \\mathrm{CO}_2(\\mathrm{~g})+\\mathrm{Y} \\mathrm{kJ} \\mathrm{mol}^{-1}$\nC (graphite) $+\\mathrm{O}_2(\\mathrm{~g}) \\rightarrow \\mathrm{CO}_2(\\mathrm{~g})+\\mathrm{Z} \\mathrm{kJ} \\mathrm{mol}^{-1}$\nat constant temperature. Then"}, "options": [{"id": "e1c8b6", "text": "X=-Y+Z", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f97e3e37d7ebba3bc4d"}, {"id": "424ce0", "text": "-X=Y+Z", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f97e3e37d7ebba3bc4e"}, {"id": "908755", "text": "X=Y+Z", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f97e3e37d7ebba3bc4f"}, {"id": "d71aaa", "text": "X=Y-Z", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f97e3e37d7ebba3bc50"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f97e3e37d7ebba3bc51", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0df8c"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b476e"], "concepts": ["60e2fb5666f9ce3f243b4f1a"], "question": {"text": "During compression of a spring the work done is <math><mn>10</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">k</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">J</mi></math> and <math><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">k</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">J</mi></math> escaped to the surroundings as heat. The change in internal energy, <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#916;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">U</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mtext>&#8201;</mtext><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">k</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">J</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> is:"}, "options": [{"id": "0b7833", "text": "<math><mo>-</mo><mn>8</mn></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f97e3e37d7ebba3bc52"}, {"id": "3aff57", "text": "<math><mn>8</mn></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f97e3e37d7ebba3bc53"}, {"id": "79b55c", "text": "<math><mn>12</mn></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f97e3e37d7ebba3bc54"}, {"id": "f18342", "text": "<math><mo>-</mo><mn>12</mn></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f97e3e37d7ebba3bc55"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f97e3e37d7ebba3bc56", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0df8c"], "topics": ["60e5671c499d1e49588f8808"], "concepts": ["60e56739499d1e49588f8b65"], "question": {"text": "For the chemical reaction $\\mathrm{X} \\rightleftharpoons \\mathrm{Y},$ the standard reaction Gibbs energy depends on temperature $T$ (in $K$ )\n\nas $\\Delta_{\\mathrm{r}} \\mathrm{G}^{\\circ}\\left(\\right.$ in $\\left.\\mathrm{kJ} \\mathrm{mol}^{-1}\\right)=120-\\frac{3}{8} \\mathrm{~T}$\n\nThe major component of the reaction mixture at $\\mathrm{T}$ is :"}, "options": [{"id": "887244", "text": "$Y$ if $T=300 K$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f97e3e37d7ebba3bc57"}, {"id": "db8809", "text": "$\\mathrm{Y}$ if $\\mathrm{T}=280 \\mathrm{~K}$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f97e3e37d7ebba3bc58"}, {"id": "5b43fe", "text": "X if $T=350 \\mathrm{~K}$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f97e3e37d7ebba3bc59"}, {"id": "fc7a35", "text": "$X$ if $T=315 K$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f97e3e37d7ebba3bc5a"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f97e3e37d7ebba3bc5b", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0df8c"], "topics": ["60e2fb2066f9ce3f243b4b70"], "concepts": ["6117b8e067dbe2603c3e8ad2"], "question": {"text": "The process with negative entropy change is:"}, "options": [{"id": "716200", "text": "Synthesis of ammonia from <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>.", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f97e3e37d7ebba3bc5c"}, {"id": "6299ba", "text": "Dissolution of iodine in water.", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f97e3e37d7ebba3bc5d"}, {"id": "a81013", "text": "Dissociation of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>CaSO</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><mo>&#160;</mo><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></mfenced></math> to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>CaO</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></mfenced></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>SO</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>&#160;</mo><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></mfenced></math>.", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f97e3e37d7ebba3bc5e"}, {"id": "0c1f57", "text": "Sublimation of dry ice.", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f97e3e37d7ebba3bc5f"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f97e3e37d7ebba3bc60", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0df8c"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b476e"], "concepts": ["60e2fb1f66f9ce3f243b4b48"], "question": {"text": "Arrange the following in order of magnitude of work done by the system / on the system at constant temperature :<br />(a) $\\left|\\mathrm{w}_{\\text {reversible }}\\right|$ for expansion in infinite stage.<br />(b) $\\left|w_{\\text {irreversible }}\\right|$ for expansion in single stage.<br />(c) $\\left|w_{\\text {reversible }}\\right|$ for compression in infinite stage.<br />(d) $\\left|w_{\\text {irreversible }}\\right|$ for compression in single stage.<br />Choose the correct answer from the options given below:"}, "options": [{"id": "8e695c", "text": "$a \\gt b \\gt c \\gt d$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f97e3e37d7ebba3bc61"}, {"id": "c7ee15", "text": "$d \\gt c=a \\gt b$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f97e3e37d7ebba3bc62"}, {"id": "e4b1b8", "text": "$c=a \\gt d \\gt b$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f97e3e37d7ebba3bc63"}, {"id": "10bdbe", "text": "$a \\gt c \\gt b \\gt d$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f97e3e37d7ebba3bc64"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f97e3e37d7ebba3bc65", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0df8c"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b4783"], "concepts": ["6117b5e4478ae845c43c5e1c"], "question": {"text": "Given below are two statements :<br />Statement I : When a system containing ice in equilibrium with water (liquid) is heated, heat is absorbed by the system and there is no change in the temperature of the system until whole ice gets melted.<br />Statement II : At melting point of ice, there is absorption of heat in order to overcome intermolecular forces of attraction within the molecules of water in ice and kinetic energy of molecules is not increased at melting point.<br />In the light of the above statements, choose the correct answer from the options given below:"}, "options": [{"id": "733903", "text": "Statement I is true but Statement II is false", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f97e3e37d7ebba3bc66"}, {"id": "a5da33", "text": "Both Statement I and Statement II are false", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f97e3e37d7ebba3bc67"}, {"id": "02d725", "text": "Both Statement I and Statement II are true", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f97e3e37d7ebba3bc68"}, {"id": "8266c0", "text": "Statement I is false but Statement II is true", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f97e3e37d7ebba3bc69"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f97e3e37d7ebba3bc6a", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0df8c"], "topics": ["60e5671c499d1e49588f8808"], "concepts": ["60e5671a499d1e49588f87ea"], "question": {"text": "Let us consider a reversible reaction at temperature, T.<br />In this reaction, both $\\Delta \\mathrm{H}$ and $\\Delta \\mathrm{S}$ were observed to have positive values. If the equilibrium temperature is Te , then the reaction becomes spontaneous at :"}, "options": [{"id": "cc8b83", "text": "$\\mathrm{T}=\\mathrm{Te}$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f97e3e37d7ebba3bc6b"}, {"id": "c8314c", "text": "$\\mathrm{Te} \\gt \\mathrm{T}$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f97e3e37d7ebba3bc6c"}, {"id": "c24f93", "text": "$\\mathrm{T} \\gt \\mathrm{Te}$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f97e3e37d7ebba3bc6d"}, {"id": "f936bb", "text": "$\\mathrm{Te}=5 \\mathrm{~T}$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f97e3e37d7ebba3bc6e"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f97e3e37d7ebba3bc6f", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0df8c"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b4783"], "concepts": ["6176f3ee6581241c7072a758"], "question": {"text": "Given:<br /><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i</mi></mfenced></math> <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mtext>C</mtext><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mi>graphite</mi></mfenced><mo>+</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></mfenced><mo>&#8594;</mo><msub><mi>CO</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></mfenced><mo>;</mo></math> <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>&#916;rH</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#920;</mi></msup><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mi>kJ</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><msup><mi>mol</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math><br /><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mi>ii</mi></mfenced></math> <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mi>graphite</mi></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></mfenced><mo>&#8594;</mo><mi>CO</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></mfenced><mo>&#160;;</mo></math> <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>&#916;rH</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#920;</mi></msup><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">y</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mi>kJ</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><msup><mi>mol</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math><br /><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mi>iii</mi></mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mi>CO</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></mfenced><mo>&#8594;</mo><msub><mi>CO</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></mfenced><mo>;</mo></math> <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>&#916;rH</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#920;</mi></msup><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">z</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mi>kJ</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><msup><mi>mol</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math><br /><br />Based on the above thermochemical equations, find out which one of the following algebraic relationships is correct?"}, "options": [{"id": "d65959", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">y</mi><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">z</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f97e3e37d7ebba3bc70"}, {"id": "b38393", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">z</mi><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">y</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f97e3e37d7ebba3bc71"}, {"id": "e20f88", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">z</mi><mo>-</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f97e3e37d7ebba3bc72"}, {"id": "d87ac1", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\