\\mathrm{H}_{2} \\mathrm{O} \\rightleftharpoons \\mathrm{H}_{3} \\mathrm{O}^{+}+\\mathrm{OH}^{-} ;$ the value of $\\Delta \\mathrm{G}^{\\circ}$ at $298 \\mathrm{~K}$ is approximately:"}, "options": [{"id": "10ed27", "text": "$100 \\mathrm{~kJ} \\mathrm{~mol}^{-1}$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f97e3e37d7ebba3bc7a"}, {"id": "bd1604", "text": "$-80 \\mathrm{~kJ} \\mathrm{~mol}^{-1}$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f97e3e37d7ebba3bc7b"}, {"id": "c7d665", "text": "$80 \\mathrm{~kJ} \\mathrm{~mol}^{-1}$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f97e3e37d7ebba3bc7c"}, {"id": "1a99a5", "text": "$-100 \\mathrm{~kJ} \\mathrm{~mol}^{-1}$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f97e3e37d7ebba3bc7d"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f97e3e37d7ebba3bc7e", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0df8c"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b476e"], "concepts": ["60e2fb5666f9ce3f243b4f22"], "question": {"text": "Consider the reversible isothermal expansion of an ideal gas in a closed system at two different temperatures <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>&#60;</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced></math> . The correct graphical depiction of the dependence of work done <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">w</mi></mfenced></math>&nbsp;vs&nbsp;the final volume <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></mfenced></math> is:"}, "options": [{"id": "734461", "text": "<p><img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_main%2F51ef96a0-e5ed-4a3e-a30f-97c